Author: CusDeb OS Team
Description: winex11: Export a window icon of the size the window manager draws.
 _NET_WM_ICON carries the big and small window icons (64 and 32 pixels at
 192 DPI). Openbox draws the title bar icon at the height of its title
 font, 40 pixels there, and scales the 64 pixel icon down, which blurs
 it. The new X11 Driver registry option TitleIconSize names that size;
 an icon of that size is loaded from the icon's resource and exported
 too, so the window manager does not scale. A resource without an entry
 of that size gives its next larger entry scaled by user32. Without the
 option nothing changes.
 .
 Icons that do not come from a resource are left to the window manager.
 CopyImage can only stretch them without a filter, and the result is
 worse than the window manager's scaling (seen at 192 DPI with a 64 pixel
 folder icon reduced to 40).
